<title>COLOMBIA: TABLE-Banco Bogota posts 74.6 pct rise in 1H net.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Banco Bogota posts 74.6 pct rise in 1H net.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's Banco de Bogota, part of the Sarmiento Angulo financial group, posted the following first-half results:</p>
<p>    First-half 1997			    First-half 1996</p>
<p> Net profits 70.1 bln pesos		   Profits 40.1 bln</p>
<p> Profit per share 404 pesos		   Per share 251</p>
<p> Operational revenues 367.9 bln pesos     Op. Revs. 296.8 bln</p>
<p> Total assets 2.8 trillion pesos	    Assets 2.3 trillion</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in Colombian pesos and are subject to review by the Securities Superintendency.</p>
<p>((--Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
